  "prefLabel": "Pda 101.33 Slip",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pda 101.33 “Slip” means “slip” as defined in RSA 12-G:2, XXII-a, namely, “a volume of water at least 25 feet long, 8 feet wide, and 3 feet deep as measured at normal high tide and located adjacent to a structure such as a dock, wharf, or pier to which a vessel may be secured.”\n\nSource. #8760, eff 11-18-06",
